# Project development start

Owner and supported native toolchains: pending project adoption. Use
[configuration](configuration.md), [core](../agent-governance/core.md),
[architecture](../agent-governance/architecture.md),
[planning](../agent-governance/planning.md) and [testing](../quality/testing.md).

| Purpose | Working directory | Native command / inputs | Expected result and state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Setup | Project/component root | Select runtime, package manager and reviewed manifest/lock | Unconfigured; document a clean reproducible install |
| Run | Owning application root | Select the actual application entrypoint | Unconfigured; record startup/readiness and stop behavior |
| Build | Owning component root | Native compiler/build system | Unconfigured; identify actual output |
| Test | Owning component or integration root | Selected native suite | Unconfigured; preserve relevant failures and limits |
| Check | Project root and applicable components | Native lint/type/security plus external trusted starter verifier | Product checks unconfigured; structural seed PASS is limited |

The included `scripts/runner_doctor.py --profile development` checks local
prerequisites without installing tools. Run it with a supported Python interpreter.
The environment checker at `.engineering-backbone/src/environment.py` validates
only declared inputs; it does not load application settings or establish readiness.
The neutral environment register is initially empty.

## Generated outputs

Local generated outputs live under `artifacts/<tool-or-run>/`. The directory
contents are ignored and only `artifacts/README.md` is tracked. These outputs are
derived and non-authoritative: they are not requirements, design, review evidence,
PASS or approval. Keep credentials, private transcripts and personal data out of
them, and do not upload them as CI artifacts.

Obtain a separately reviewed Backbone source checkout at a fixed full Git commit,
then use isolated Python (`python -I`) with that checkout's `starter.py verify --source-ref FULL_SHA --root PROJECT`.
Its Python dependencies are installed from that trusted source's reviewed lock.
Do not run a source-history validator inside this seed. Keep product commands and
existing workflow-kit bindings in their established authoritative locations; no
second command dispatcher is installed here.

Record actual platform/runtime versions, command, exit, revision and coverage.
Optional CI, quality/navigation/dependency contracts require separately reviewed
integration; this seed includes no active workflow. Missing required execution
remains a project gate rather than a successful empty command.
